cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Sensitivity Is Not Use: code for testing whether structure-based affinity models learn from geometry"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kotan"
    given-names: "Kurban"
    affiliation: "Department of Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning, Faculty of Computer and Information Sciences, Manisa Celal Bayar University"
    email: "kurban.kotan@cbu.edu.tr"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kurbankotan/sensitivity-is-not-use"
abstract: >-
  A diagnostic protocol that separates a model's sensitivity to protein-ligand
  geometry from its use of that geometry, applied to three deep architectures and
  a contact-count positive control on leak-proof PDBbind splits.
keywords:
  - binding affinity prediction
  - structure-based drug design
  - shortcut learning
  - ablation
  - model diagnostics
